<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sargon II</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a> II was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-assyrian-empire">Neo-Assyrian Empire</a> in the late eighth century BCE, who founded a new capital at Dur-Sharrukin. His reign saw extensive campaigns across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>. The Elamite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/humban-nikash-i">Humban-nikash I</a> defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-der">Battle of Der</a> in 721 BCE, showing that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> could still challenge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sargon-ii.jpg" alt="Sargon II" width="288" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Osama Shukir Muhammed Amin FRCP(Glasg) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sargon_II,_Iraq_Museum_in_Baghdad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
